--- what the mutant is for --------------------------------------------------
Every assertion in the stopped-schema test is about something *not* happening,
so an implementation that refused every Realm at the schema boundary would
satisfy it. This mutant is that implementation. The pair below is what makes the
control a control rather than a restatement.

--- observed at this snapshot -----------------------------------------------
$ cargo test -p kontor-daemon --bin kontor-daemon -- a_realm_stopped_before_the_current_schema
  test tests::a_realm_stopped_before_the_current_schema_refuses_without_reading_or_installing ... ok
  test result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 9 filtered out
    ^ the objection, reproduced: the stopped-schema test cannot tell the difference.

$ cargo test -p kontor-daemon --bin kontor-daemon -- a_current_realm_reaches_the_credential_reader
  thread 'tests::a_current_realm_reaches_the_credential_reader_and_fails_after_the_gate'
  panicked at crates/kontor-daemon/src/main.rs:967:9:
  a current realm did not reach the credential reader: Err(CredentialScope)
  test result: FAILED. 0 passed; 1 failed; 9 filtered out
    ^ the hardened control catches it.

Exact test names at this snapshot:
  tests::a_realm_stopped_before_the_current_schema_refuses_without_reading_or_installing
  tests::a_current_realm_reaches_the_credential_reader_and_fails_after_the_gate
  tests::the_stopped_fixtures_reproduce_their_own_schema_era
